{
    "background_story": "Amiri, a majestic grizzly bear, roamed the forest with a gentle giant's stride. As winter approached, Amiri's instincts told her it was time to prepare for the long slumber. She found a secluded den, lined with leaves and twigs, and settled in for a period of torpor. For months, her heart rate slowed, and her body temperature dropped, conserving energy as the harsh winter raged on outside. During this time, Amiri's body repaired and rejuvenated itself, storing up fat reserves for the spring. When the snow finally began to melt, Amiri emerged from her den, stretching and yawning as she shook off the torpor. She ambled out into the forest, sniffing the air for signs of spring, ready to begin another year of exploring and thriving in her mountain home.",
